<%# locals: () %>
<%#
  How to read the mail log table and what its two row icons mean: two questions
  and their answers, rendered inside the page's About This Report list. Shared
  by the person and system-wide pages. Each icon is named by the word its row
  carries, because the icon itself is hidden from a screen reader, and drawn in
  the colour its row takes.
%>
<dt>How do I read a message?</dt>
<dd>Expand a subject line to view the message.</dd>
<dt>What do the icons mean?</dt>
<dd>
  <%= fa_icon "triangle-exclamation", :solid, class: "text-error" %> <%= MailLogHelper::BOUNCED_LABEL %>:
  the address doesn't exist or the mailbox is full.
  <%= fa_icon "bell", :solid, class: "text-warning" %> <%= MailLogHelper::SPAM_LABEL %>: the
  recipient's mail provider marked the email as spam.
</dd>
